    "forensics": "The losing cluster was primarily driven by morning-session liquidity traps and tight-stop whipsaws (0.4% SL), best exemplified by the October 22 cluster where four consecutive long entries failed within an hour due to weak volume confirmation (1.3x). Furthermore, Trades #6 and #8 achieved positive gross P&L before reversing to hit trailing stops, converting winning price action into net losses due to premature breakeven triggers (1.0R) and severe NSE transaction fee drag (\u20b942.12 in fees exceeding the \u20b9-25.31 net loss).",
    "learning": "In Indian NSE cash equities on a 5-minute timeframe, low-threshold volume sweeps (1.3x) during the 10:15\u201311:15 IST transition window frequently represent retail bull traps rather than institutional accumulation; overcoming statutory brokerage and STT drag on a \u20b910,000 capital base requires wider initial stop-losses to absorb intraday noise, higher volume conviction, and larger profit targets.",
    "parameter_patch": {
      "min_target_pct": 1.25,
      "min_sweep_vol_multiplier": 1.85,
      "breakeven_trigger_r": 1.25,
      "min_sl_pct": 0.55
    },
    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #27 Post-Mortem & Parameter Mutation\nOut-of-sample testing with DeepSeek V4.1 Flash yielded a 33.3% win rate and a Profit Factor of 0.74, heavily impacted by transaction fee drag (\u20b942.12 fees vs. \u20b9+16.81 gross P&L) and correlated mid-morning stop-outs (notably on Oct 22 across TATASTEEL, NTPC, and AXISBANK). Forensics revealed that the 0.40% minimum stop-loss sits inside normal 5-minute NSE order-book noise, while the 1.0R breakeven trigger prematurely choked trades (Trades #6 and #8) that were gross-profitable but net-negative after brokerage and taxes. For Cycle #28, we are mutating parameters to enforce institutional-grade selectivity: raising `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` to 1.85x to filter out low-conviction morning false breakouts, widening `min_sl_pct` to 0.55% to prevent immediate whipsaws, expanding `min_target_pct` to 1.25% to ensure winners decisively clear the NSE fee hurdle, and relaxing `breakeven_trigger_r` to 1.25R to give developing trends adequate breathing room."
